Product Team – All Data

Hi Gilang,

Thank you for your feedback.

EBITDA
We’ve identified the root cause of the data difference — it stems from differences in the depreciation and amortization calculations used in the company’s reported financial statements versus our own calculations.

Currently, we derive EBITDA through our own computation, which results in variations whenever the depreciation and amortization values differ. To address this, we’re now working on updating the process so that, whenever available, the EBITDA value will be taken directly from the company’s reported figures.

We apologize for the inconvenience and will provide an update once this fix has been fully implemented.

CPLTD
As of now, we don’t have any data about CPLTD (Current Portion of Long-Term Debt). We only have metrics for current liabilities and non-current liabilities, which the data already the same with the one in IndoPremier.

Thank you.

Best regards,
Gerald

